  "entry": "code/app/streamlit_app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load a Türkiye earthquake catalogue (synthetic demo, live USGS, or an uploaded CSV/Excel file), read summary statistics and a Gutenberg-Richter b-value, look at maps, time series and distributions, screen for statistical event-rate anomalies, count nearby exposure points around each event, and browse Sentinel-1 acquisitions, candidate pairs and processed InSAR displacement points. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
